  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "If \\(N,\\) written in base \\(2,\\) is \\(11000,\\) the integer immediately preceding \\(N,\\) written in base \\(2,\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10001\\)",
    "B": "\\(10010\\)",
    "C": "\\(10011\\)",
    "D": "\\(10110\\)",
    "E": "\\(10111\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The binary place values, from right to left, are \\(1,2,4,8,16\\). Therefore\n\\[\nN=11000_2=16+8=24.\n\\]\nThe immediately preceding integer is \\(23\\). Since\n\\[\n23=16+4+2+1,\n\\]\nits digits in the \\(16,8,4,2,1\\) places are respectively \\(1,0,1,1,1\\). Thus the predecessor is \\(10111_2\\), choice E.",
